  "title": "Plain pages are always twisted, and the Fano plane is the only twist-free plain brace",
  "subject": "Where twists sit in plain triple systems with Pfaffian incidence graphs",
  "conclusion": "Euler's formula leaves every planar cubic bipartite graph a square face away from any chosen square, where a Pfaffian signing needs an odd sign, so every plain page is twisted and every square of a plain trisum brace has three twisted branches. Since a brace's 4-cycles are nice, the Heawood graph is the only brace whose plain system is not 2-colourable.",
